# November 19, 2026: Lansingburgh (north Troy) and the standing buildings of central Troy, region troy (Troy & Lansingburgh),
# drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny. The Atlas had one place in Lansingburgh (Rensselaer Park, gone) and its
# Troy entries were mostly vanished sites and the industrial south end. This batch is mostly standing buildings.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py), the Wikipedia Register list for Rensselaer
# County (--rows), National Register forms for the Methodist Episcopal Church of Lansingburgh (16000412) and the United
# Waste Manufacturing Company Building (13000054) from NPGallery, the Lansingburgh Historical Society's pages, the HMdb
# Lion Factory marker, the Troy Public Library's hours page, St. Paul's Church's and Trinity Church Lansingburgh's own pages,
# the Kate Mullany NHS home page, the National Trust's Distinctive Destinations page, the governor's 2022 Register
# nominations release, the City of Troy's Central Lansingburgh Historic District leaflet and an Albany Business Review
# article (2024) on the Lion Factory apartments, all through tools/page.py.
